{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Report\n\nThe Gerrit LLM-Review bot does not reliably queue a review when a patch set is uploaded. The change sits with `LLM-Review = --` indefinitely, and only starts reviewing after a human/agent posts a `recheck-review` comment or force-pushes a no-op rebase.\n\n## Evidence — four reproductions, 2026-08-07\n\n1. **Change 1486 (599e):** both patch-set uploads skipped; needed a `recheck-review` comment to queue.\n2. **Change 1490 (e7a9):** no vote on upload. `recheck-review` at 11:41 -> `LLM-Review -1` at 11:44. Healthy and fast ONCE TRIGGERED.\n3. **Changes 1493 / 1496 (13b4, ccf6):** both skipped; 1493 sat 70 minutes unvoted while the bot voted on NEWER changes (1497) in the same window. A no-op rebase + re-push produced votes within 5 minutes on both.\n4. **Fleet-level:** at ~11:50, `LLM-Review = --` on 1486, 1488, 1491, 1492, 1493, 1494, 1495 simultaneously while `Verified` votes landed normally.\n\nSecond-order cost: it is INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM AN OUTAGE. The e7a9 agent concluded \"the reviewer looks down\" and STOPPED work on a completed, correct change that had in fact already been reviewed.\n\n## ROOT CAUSE (proven — see the RCA comment for the full experiment log)\n\n`reconcile_once` (`src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py:232-235`) writes its persisted cursor to `newest` — the max event time across the WHOLE fetched window — **unconditionally at the end of every pass**, with no low-water mark for candidates the pass failed to vote. Three paths `continue` without voting: `reconcile_check_error` (`:213`), `review_timeout` (`:227-228`), and a voter `deferred`/`error` return. Because the events-log `?t1=` window filters SERVER-SIDE (proven live: `t1=13:00:00` returns `oldest=13:00:18`), those events are excluded from every future window — permanently.\n\nSince Gerrit's `webhooks` plugin is at-**most**-once (plugin `PostTask.run()` logs SEVERE and discards after `maxTries`; contradicting the \"at-least-once\" claim at `docs/adr/0009-review-bot-pipe.md:82`) and the receiver 202-ACKs into an in-memory queue that a container recreation discards (`app.py:112`, `:135-143`), the reconciler is the ONLY recovery path — and it blinds itself.\n\nRuntime proof (3 passes, fake events-log honouring `since`, middle candidate times out):\n```\nPASS 1: window=[Iaaa,Ibbb,Iccc] result={scanned:2,reviewed:1} cursor=10:53:50\nPASS 2: window=[Iccc]           result={scanned:0,reviewed:0} cursor=10:53:50\nPASS 3: window=[Iccc]           result={scanned:0,reviewed:0} cursor=10:53:50\n```\n\nThis is why BOTH nudges work: each mints a NEW events-log event AFTER the cursor, re-admitting the change to the window. Nothing else does.\n\nContracts violated: `reconcile.py:1-10` (\"This poller closes that loop\"), `reconcile.py:218-220` (\"is retried next pass\"), `docs/adr/0009-review-bot-pipe.md:111` (\"the reconciler is what recovers a dropped webhook\"), `docs/review-policy.md:65` (\"re-drives it automatically within its interval\").\n\nWhy it shipped: the guarding test double records `since` and then ignores it (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:682-687`), so the production cursor filter is never exercised by `test_deferred_change_stays_eligible_for_reconciler` (`:1878`) or `test_reconcile_once_times_out_a_hung_review_and_continues` (`:1392`).\n\n## Fix plan\n\n1. **`src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py` — cursor low-water mark (the root-cause fix).** Track the oldest event time among candidates the pass did NOT successfully vote (check-error, review-timeout, and any non-`voted` voter status). Clamp the persisted cursor to strictly before that time, so those candidates re-enter the next window and are re-driven, exactly as the docstring promises. Candidates that DID vote, and all non-candidate chatter, still advance the cursor — so the window does not grow without bound. Idempotency is unchanged: the dedup ledger plus the authoritative Gerrit `has_llm_review_vote` check still make a re-drive a no-op when a vote already exists.\n2. **`src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py` — make the abandonment observable.** `reconcile_done` currently reports only `scanned`/`reviewed`. Add the count of candidates the pass left un-voted and the cursor value it held back to, so \"backfill is carrying N stalled changes\" is greppable rather than silent.\n3. **`src/rebar/review_bot/app.py` — expose queue depth on `/health` (AC5).** `/health` reports only `in_flight`, so an agent cannot distinguish \"not queued\" from \"queued behind N\" from \"bot down\". Add `queue_depth` alongside the existing `in_flight` field — the same load-bearing-observable precedent that field already set for the autodeploy drain (bug 34cd).\n4. **`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` — repair the false-green double and add the RED tests.** Make the fake `list_events` HONOUR `since` (matching the proven live server semantics) so the existing AC5 test actually exercises the cursor path, and add a multi-event-window regression test in which a non-newest candidate fails and must still be re-driven on the next pass.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause established for why the upload event does not queue a review — proven, not inferred (runtime experiment + live events-log probe; see RCA comment)\n- [ ] A patch-set upload that the webhook drops is re-driven WITHOUT any manual comment, proven by a test that drives two reconcile passes against a `since`-honouring events-log and asserts the un-voted candidate is re-driven on pass 2\n- [ ] If the trigger can still fail, the failure is OBSERVABLE — the count of candidates backfill is carrying is emitted per pass rather than being silent\n- [ ] `recheck-review` remains available as a manual override, but is no longer the routine path\n- [ ] The distinction between 'not queued', 'queued and running', and 'reviewed' is visible to an agent or human inspecting the change (`/health` gains `queue_depth` next to `in_flight`)"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786116065964730001,"uuid":"e83aec00-d90a-41a1-ae2a-7b3451ea468d"}